   },
   {
    "text": "It has been described as the most alien-looking place on Earth.",
    "shot": "feature",
    "overlay": {
     "type": "highlight",
     "on": "place"
    },
    "react": {
     "expr": "happy",
     "on": "place"
    },
    "photo": null
   },
   {
    "text": "Locally, it's known as Saqatri.",
    "shot": "close",
    "overlay": {
     "type": "tag",
     "on": "Saqatri",
     "label": "KNOWN AS SAQATRI"
    },
    "react": null,
    "photo": null
   },
   {
    "text": "Lay Luxembourg over it, and the island still runs past both ends.",
    "shot": "feature",
    "overlay": {
     "type": "scale",
     "on": "Luxembourg"
    },
    "react": null,
    "photo": null
   },
   {
    "text": "It belongs to Yemen, but geologically it's a fragment of Africa.",
    "shot": "wide",
    "overlay": {
     "type": "tag",
     "on": "fragment",
     "label": "FRAGMENT OF AFRICA"
    },
    "react": {
     "expr": "surprised",
     "on": "Africa"
    },
    "photo": null
   },
   {
    "text": "Two hundred thirty-two kilometers of sea and a long isolation did the rest.",
    "shot": "wide",
    "overlay": null,
    "react": null,
    "photo": null
   },
   {
    "text": "In two thousand eight, it became a UNESCO World Heritage Site.",
